Chapter: DeskPaneOriginTest
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopFiles
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Layout
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Four chapters used to restate where the desk's sidebar ends, in three unit
 systems, and the Files pane painted 140 device pixels inside it at 1600 and
 sliced every sidebar button in half. Every pane is a window now and the
 sidebar is gone, so the number those chapters disagreed about no longer
 exists -- but the QUESTION it was asked for does, and it is the one asserted
 here: a pane's rectangle must never overlap anything the chrome draws.

 RE-POINTED TWICE, AND NEITHER TIME SOFTENED (L-INSTRUMENT). It first compared
 the Files panel's origin against `ui-sidebar-px`; then the content box's,
 when every pane became a window; and now the laid CONTENT SLOT against the
 content box, because with the sidebar deleted `ui-sidebar-px` is not a
 function any more. The subject moved each time and the question did not.

 IT IS AN ASSERTION AGAINST THE CONTRACT, NOT AGAINST ANOTHER INSTANCE OF THE
 SAME ARITHMETIC (L-BOTHARMS). The box comes from `dk-cbox-x` and its three
 siblings; the slot comes from `widget-layout` walking the real chrome tree
 and reaching a rectangle through `widget-measure`, the panel minima and the
 theme's padding. Two routes, and containment is what they must agree on. A
 row comparing either against itself would pass under any defect.

 It held BEFORE the sidebar was deleted and it holds after, which is the point
 of writing it against the contract: at 1600 the chrome laid its content slot
 at 336 device pixels inside a box starting at 320, and it lays it at 16
 inside a box starting at 0. Both are contained. A left gutter re-introduced
 without telling `dk-cbox-x` about it moves the slot out of the box and this
 goes red, which is exactly the WORKS-35 class.

 BOTH WIDTHS ARE REQUIRED AND ONE IS NOT ENOUGH. `ui-scale` steps at 1024 and
 `ui-wscale` at 1600, so the two AGREE at 1600 and disagree from 1024 to 1599.
 Every wrong version of the old constant was right at one of these widths and
 that is why the defect survived a single-width arm for as long as it did.

 The face is `gfont-none` deliberately: `gfont-load` needs a volume, the
 battery attaches none, and `desk-chrome-with` is the faceless path the
 sibling arms already use for that reason (L-NAMED).

Section: Body

  dpo-yn : Boolean -> Text
  dpo-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "NO"

  dpo-chrome : Integer, Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  dpo-chrome (w) (h) (ds) =
    let s = ui-wscale w
    in widget-layout (desk-chrome-with (widget-panel "content" DirColumn 0 []) w ds) (dk-theme-ds ds) (layout-rect 0 0 (w / s) (h / s))

  dpo-slot : WidgetNode, Text -> LayoutRect
  dpo-slot (laid) (id) =
    when widget-find laid id
      is Just (n) -> n.wn-bounds
      is None -> layout-rect 0 0 0 0

 The slot is laid in LOGICAL units and the box answers DEVICE pixels, which is
 the mismatch `ui-sidebar-px` existed to stop four chapters getting wrong in
 three different directions. One multiply, in one place.

  dpo-row : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  dpo-row (w) (h) (ds) =
    let s = ui-wscale w
    in let slot = dpo-slot (dpo-chrome w h ds) "content"
    in let sx = slot.lr-x * s
    in let sy = slot.lr-y * s
    in let sr = (slot.lr-x + slot.lr-w) * s
    in let sb = (slot.lr-y + slot.lr-h) * s
    in let bx = dk-cbox-x w
    in let by = dk-cbox-y w
    in let br = bx + dk-cbox-w w
    in let bb = by + dk-cbox-h w h ds
    in "w " & integer-to-text w
       & "  slot " & integer-to-text sx & "," & integer-to-text sy
       & " to " & integer-to-text sr & "," & integer-to-text sb
       & "  box " & integer-to-text bx & "," & integer-to-text by
       & " to " & integer-to-text br & "," & integer-to-text bb
       & "  slot inside box " & dpo-yn (sx >= bx & sy >= by & sr <= br & sb <= bb)

 The welcome window is centred in the content area by a different route than
 the panes take, so it gets its own row rather than riding theirs.

  dpo-win : Integer, Integer -> Text
  dpo-win (w) (h) =
    let s = ui-scale w
    in "w " & integer-to-text w
       & "  window x " & integer-to-text (dk-win-x w s)
       & "  inside the box " & dpo-yn (dk-win-x w s >= dk-cbox-x w & dk-win-x w s + dk-win-w * s <= dk-cbox-x w + dk-cbox-w w)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let ds = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let ap = poke-32 ds dk-adorn-cell dk-adorn-default
    in act
      print-line-uni (dpo-row 1280 800 ds)
      print-line-uni (dpo-row 1600 900 ds)
      print-line-uni (dpo-win 1280 800)
      print-line-uni (dpo-win 1600 900)
    end

